Security/no-claim proof:

- Risk detection candidates require evidence refs and source refs.
- Unknown executable names and hash-derived rows remain heuristic/review
  candidates, not source truth.
- Unknown publisher state must keep confidence at review level.
- Local AI rows must cite a digest and cannot directly enforce.
- Parent overrides can change display/routing only and cannot mutate raw app
  identity.
- Every row carries `notDirectEnforcement: true` and `noContentClaim: true`.
- Risk app policy targets require category proof before policy compilation.
- No screen, keystroke, chat, voice, network payload, private path content, or
  app content capture claim is made.
